                <pb facs="0507" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg423"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Tower.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-18"><hi rendition="#italic">December 18,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the United States minister to Venezuela telegraphs that the
                    Government of Venezuela confers upon him full powers to enter into negotiations
                    on the part of Venezuela to settle the present difficulties with Germany, Great
                    Britain, and Italy.</p>
                <p>Mr. Tower is instructed to communicate the Venezuelan proposition to the
                    Government of Germany, and ascertain if it is disposed to assent thereto.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
